				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				110,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Vine): Consolidate notification mod.rs to retain only non-trivial handlers\n\nRemove pure-relay notification modules that perform single-step delegation (OutputAppend, OutputChannelClear/Create/Dispose/Replace/Show, OutputClear/Create/Dispose, ProgressComplete/Update, WindowShowTextDocument, WorkspaceApplyEdit, ExtensionActivated/Deactivated, TreeRefresh, ExtensionHostMessage, LanguagesSetDocumentLanguage, WebviewReady) which are now inlined directly in Mountain's dispatcher.\n\nUpdate module documentation to clarify the retention criteria: handlers must have payload reshaping, channel-drain coalescing, multiple side effects, or non-obvious Sky-event mapping. Retain OutputChannelCoalesce and ProgressStart/End/Report as they implement channel-drain coalescers.\n\nThis reduction from ~45 to ~20 modules streamlines the notification surface while preserving all handlers with genuine orchestration complexity.",
			"SHA": "74f76952aeba7c2b4f442c7ce9d1a54d169bfb66"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T14:08:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				110,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Vine): Inline trivial provider unregistration atoms\n\nRemove the wrapper modules `UnregisterFileSystemProvider` and `UnregisterUriHandler` from the notification tree. These atoms performed only single-step delegation to `UnregisterByHandle` with scheme logging, which is now handled directly in Mountain's dispatcher.\n\nRetain `UnregisterScmProvider` as it contains the DJB-31 handle recomputation logic, `UnregisterProvider` call, Sky event relay, and detailed logging.\n\nThis consolidates the unregistration surface to only expose atoms with genuine multi-step orchestration needs.",
			"SHA": "a254bd2d8976d0b8d403199a9ee908b7eddaa60f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T13:52:28Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				110,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Add webview lifecycle notification handler and SCM group marker persistence\n\nImplement `WebviewLifecycle` notification to canonicalize Cocoon's positional `[Handle, Value]` arrays into named-key objects before emitting to Sky renderer channels (`sky://webview/*`). This mirrors the reshape logic in `Track/Effect/CreateEffectForRequest/Webview.rs` and supports `setTitle`, `setIconPath`, `setHtml`, `postMessage`, `updateView`, `viewState`, and `dispose` operations.\n\nAdd `UpdateScmGroup` notification to persist SCM resource-state snapshots via `VineHost::UpdateScmGroupMarkers` for boot-time replay, while also emitting `sky://scm/updateGroup` events for live UI updates. The handler resolves handles from both the new `scmHandle`/`groupHandle` format and legacy `providerId`/`groupId` keys.\n\nExtend the `VineHost` trait with `UpdateScmGroupMarkers` to allow embedders to checkpoint SCM marker state without blocking the notification path.\n\nThese changes complete the webview mediation layer and ensure SCM viewlet state survives page reloads.",
			"SHA": "df4fc467893c335a90de21aa162c0579ae53883d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T13:46:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				108,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Vine): Streamline provider unregistration modules and add scheme logging\n\nSimplify the notification module structure in `mod.rs` by removing explicit module declarations for providers that delegate directly to `UnregisterByHandle` (authentication, debug_adapter, debug_configuration, external_uri_opener, remote_authority_resolver, task). Add a clarifying comment explaining this design choice.\n\nEnhance `UnregisterFileSystemProvider` with scheme logging via `dev_log!` to record the bound scheme during unregistration. This aids in diagnosing routing mismatches after provider disposal.\n\nThese changes complete the cleanup of the provider unregistration surface, reducing file count while preserving all unregistration pathways and improving observability.",
			"SHA": "bb37f7446c8d620b0dbdd85560fca5b0fe5cc1e7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T13:37:16Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				108,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Implement provider unregistration handlers for remote authority, SCM, task, and URI types\n\nComplete the symmetrical provider lifecycle in the Vine notification layer by adding unregistration counterparts to the existing registration infrastructure.\n\nNew modules:\n- `UnregisterRemoteAuthorityResolver`: cleanup for remote authority providers\n- `UnregisterScmProvider`: handles both explicit handle and DJB-31 hash derivation from scmId to match registration strategy\n- `UnregisterTaskProvider`: task provider disposal\n- `UnregisterUriHandler`: URI scheme handler deregistration with scheme logging\n\nAll handlers integrate with the central `UnregisterByHandle` utility to guarantee consistent handle removal from the provider registry and emit appropriate renderer-side events to maintain UI state.\n\nThis completes the provider manageability surface, enabling Cocoon extensions to cleanly dispose resources without leaving dangling handles, and preserving the union-type target invariant on the embedder side.",
			"SHA": "8bd3ccb739063d2c2b45bb20d678c078d2c57a36"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1782655469841
